summary:
  The next page is asked from the number of rows on screen.

history:
  The offset was the row count plus a correction kept beside it. The count
  moves with every star and stands behind the directory's own position by
  every row the dedup dropped, so a page was asked from a place the list had
  already passed. The popup keeps the place the last walk reached and asks
  from there; SearchLogic.pageAfter moves it.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FullRepresentation.qml

find:
          root._rbFetch(fullRepresentation._webLastQs + "&offset=" + from, 4000, function(xhr) {

replace:
          root._rbFetch(fullRepresentation._webLastQs + "&offset=" + webResultsModel.count, 4000, function(xhr) {

